  {
    "title": "Four-way endings use i, ı, ü or u to match the word",
    "body": "Many endings, such as the past tense -di, have four forms. After e or i you hear i, after a or ı you hear ı, after ö or ü you hear ü, after o or u you hear u. After p, ç, t, k, f, h, s, ş the d of the ending turns into t.",
    "pattern": "(?<=\\p{L}{2})(?<!(?<!\\p{L})(?:şim|bü|al|ken|ye|yar|ka|kö|ku|cid))[dt][ıiuü](?:m|n|k|l[ae]r|n[ıiuü]z)?(?!\\p{L})",
    "examples": [
      {
        "word": "geldi",
        "say": "gel-DEE",
        "en": "came"
      },
      {
        "word": "aldı",
        "say": "ahl-DUH",
        "en": "took, bought"
      },
