        "say": "dee-YER",
        "en": "other"
      },
      {
        "word": "yemeği",
        "say": "yeh-meh-YEE",
        "en": "his or her food"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "de and da meaning “too” are never stressed",
    "body": "Written as a separate word, de or da means “too, also” or “and”. It follows harmony but never turns into te or ta, and it leans on the word before it without stress. Compare evde “ev-DEH”, at home.",
    "pattern": "(?<!\\p{L})d[ae](?!\\p{L})",
    "examples": [
      {
        "word": "ben de",
        "say": "BEN deh",
        "en": "me too"
