        "en": "he or she too"
      },
      {
        "word": "ailem de",
        "say": "ah-ee-LEM deh",
        "en": "my family too"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "ğ before a consonant or at the end makes the vowel long",
    "body": "ğ, the “soft g”, is never said as “g”. After a vowel and before a consonant or the end of the word, it simply stretches the vowel before it. After e it can sound like a faint “y”: eğlence “ey-len-JEH”.",
    "pattern": "(?<=[aeıioöuü])ğ(?![aeıioöuü])",
    "examples": [
      {
        "word": "dağ",
        "say": "daa",
        "en": "mountain"
      },
      {
        "word": "yağmur",
        "say": "yaa-MOOR",
        "en": "rain"
