      {
        "word": "sağlık",
        "say": "saa-LUHK",
        "en": "health"
      },
      {
        "word": "öğretmen",
        "say": "öö-ret-MEN",
        "en": "teacher"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Endings for “am, are, is” and -le are not stressed",
    "body": "Personal endings such as -(y)ım “I am”, the ending -dır “is”, and -le “with” don't take the stress: it stays on the syllable before them.",
    "pattern": "(?<=[aeıioöuüâîû])(?<!(?<!\\p{L})(?:gi|dene))y[ıiuü]m(?!\\p{L})|(?<=\\p{L}{3})(?<!kül)[dt][ıiuü]r(?!\\p{L})|(?<=\\p{L}{2}[^\\P{L}aeıioöuüâîûl])(?<!(?<!\\p{L})(?:faz|dam|tav|cüm|ley|böy|şöy))l[ae](?!\\p{L})",
    "examples": [
