  {
    "title": "Negative -me and -ma pull the stress before them",
    "body": "In verbs, the negative ending -me or -ma is never stressed: the syllable just before it is. So geldi is “gel-DEE” but gelmedi is “GEL-meh-dee”.",
    "pattern": "(?<=\\p{L}{2})(?:m[ae]d[ıi]|m[ıiuü]yor|m[ae]y[ae]c[ae][kğ]|(?<!yıl)m[ae]z(?!\\p{L}))",
    "examples": [
